course: dictionary
lesson: 3143
title: Email: a thing and an action
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An email is a message sent from one computer or phone to another over the internet. It is a thing you can count, read and reply to. «Ava read Mum's emails and found out about a surprise trip» tells you that emails are things you can read, and that there can be more than one.
explain: Email also has a verb form, so you can do it. To email means to send an email. «I will email you the photos tonight» uses email as an action. Try the meaning in the sentence: "I will send a message over the internet to you tonight." It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Some words come up again and again with email. Look at the words around them: send an email, get an email, reply to an email, email address. In «Fake emails often come from strange addresses that only look a little like the real company», the clue is strange addresses, so you can guess that an email address is where a message is sent to.
fact: An email is a message sent over the internet from one computer or phone to another.
fact: Email can be a noun, as in «Ava read Mum's emails», or a verb, as in «I will email you».
fact: Useful phrases are send an email, get an email, reply to an email and email address.
fact: «Fake emails» often use a strange address that only looks a little like the real company's.
fact: «Spelling mistakes», odd email addresses and rushing you are clues that a message may be fake, so check before you click.
exercise: «Ava read Mum's emails and found out about a surprise trip.» What is an email in this sentence? | A phone call with no words | A photo album | A paper letter in an envelope | *A message sent over the internet
exercise: «Fake emails often come from strange addresses that only look a little like the real company.» What is one clue that an email may be fake? | A reply to an email you sent | A message from your best friend | A photo of your family | *A strange address that only looks like the real company's
exercise: To email means to send an email. Which word fits? «I will ___ you the photos tonight.» | address | emails | *email | emailed
test: Which phrase means to send a message back to an email you got? | email address | send an email | get an email | *reply to an email
test: According to «different passwords stop one leak opening everything», why should you use different passwords? | So emails stop coming | *So one leak does not open everything | So your emails arrive faster | So you can forget them easily
exam: «Spelling mistakes, odd email addresses and rushing you are clues that a message is fake.» Which option lists these clues? | *Spelling mistakes, odd email addresses and rushing you | Spelling you can read easily and kind words | Emails sent in the morning and in the evening | A long greeting and a nice picture
